  },
  "fixture_and_handoff_observations": {
    "export_staging": "The replacement refused an unresolved published staging entry. Passing runs resolved the publication with the original helper, verified staging and reservation release, and kept the completed export receipt across the upgrade.",
    "record_comparison": "A first checkpoint witness reached a different helper epoch and retained its completed capture. Comparing next_due_at_ms as immutable caused its assertion to fail. The corrected comparison checked all remaining fields and ordinary cleanup.",
    "volume_root": "The earlier scratch-root fixture was refused. Passing runs used the canonical SDK volume root and verified the retained attachment, guest file, exact deletion, and reservation release.",
    "linux_branch_history": "Fresh branch attempts returned an unknown child-creation outcome before helper replacement. Both replacement toolchains instead opened independent cold PostgreSQL copies of the previously completed ordinary Linux branch history from embedded-port-http-parity-durable-workflows-3d15db7b.json. The current toolchain originally wrote that history. The original cluster stayed stopped.",
    "lab_memory": "The Linux provisioning VM used temporary compressed swap after the earlier retained test scopes reduced available memory."
  },
